{
 "about": "The Cassini narrow-angle frames of Titan, calibrated to I/F with CISSCAL, from the PDS Ring-Moon Systems Node (OPUS): four sets in its blue, green and red filters, taken in January and February 2010, months after Titan's equinox. The geometry is from the volume's index table: latitudes planetocentric and longitudes east, distance to Titan's centre, resolution in km a pixel at the sub-spacecraft point, and the north clock angle, from up in the frame to Titan's pole as projected, measured clockwise.",
